// The game's own help text, in English. A topic number is the one the screens' help areas name
// (`help_screens.ron`). A topic that is not here opens nothing.
[
    (index: 216, title: "Game", text: "Opens the save and load screen. From there you can also change the settings or leave the game."),
    (index: 217, title: "Spells", text: "Opens your spell book, from which you cast overland spells. Spells for battle are cast in the battle itself."),
    (index: 218, title: "Armies", text: "Lists all of your stacks of units. Pick one to centre the map on it, or open a unit's sheet."),
    (index: 219, title: "Cities", text: "Lists all of your cities with their size, what they are building and what they produce. Pick one to open it."),
    (index: 220, title: "Magic", text: "Opens your magic screen: how your power is split between mana, research and casting skill, what you are casting and researching, and the enchantments you keep up."),
    (index: 221, title: "Information", text: "Opens the list of advisors: the Surveyor, Cartographer, Apprentice, Historian, Astrologer, Chancellor, Tax Collector, Grand Vizier and the Mirror."),
    (index: 222, title: "Plane", text: "Switches the map between Arcanus and Myrror. With units selected, the units change plane instead if they are standing where they can (a tower of wizardry, or a plane gate)."),
    (index: 223, title: "Done", text: "Cancels the orders of the selected units, such as a march in progress, so they stay where they are. The keyboard shortcut is D."),
    (index: 225, title: "Wait", text: "Puts the selected stack aside for now and selects the next stack that still has moves left. The stack comes back later in the turn. The keyboard shortcut is W."),
    (index: 226, title: "Build", text: "The special action of the selected units: settlers found a city, engineers build a road, a unit that can purify cleanses corrupted land, and a spirit melds with a magic node. The keyboard shortcut is B."),
    (index: 229, title: "Next turn", text: "Ends your turn once no unit is left waiting for orders. The other wizards then play, and the next turn begins."),
    (index: 231, title: "Gold", text: "The gold in your treasury. Gold pays for buildings and units you buy, and for upkeep."),
    (index: 232, title: "Mana", text: "The mana in your reserve. Mana pays for spells, for the upkeep of the spells you keep up, and for summoned creatures."),
    (index: 233, title: "Gold income", text: "The gold you gain or lose each turn: the taxes of your cities less the upkeep of buildings and units. If the treasury cannot pay, you are asked which units to let go before the turn ends."),
    (index: 234, title: "Food", text: "The food your cities produce each turn less what your units eat. If it is negative, you are asked which units to let go before the turn ends."),
    (index: 235, title: "Mana income", text: "The mana you gain or lose each turn: what your cities and nodes produce, less the upkeep of the spells you keep up. A negative figure drains your reserve; when the reserve runs out, you are asked which spells to give up."),
    (index: 236, title: "Moves", text: "How many moves the selected units have left this turn. A stack moves at the speed of its slowest unit."),
]
